35,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The receipts show 2,300 yen monthly, with duplicate purchases. The management bill is 4,200 yen per hour. We need a clear cost structure.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"@Toshio, the timing is worse than I feared. A full pass is over two hours. The firm’s two-hour window means we must be home and tidy beforehand.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Ryuji, two hours is brutal. My data shows two people are gone weekly, yet the kitchen mess is from just three. We need to match labor to presence.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, that explains the chaos. My findings show ""done"" means different things to everyone, and the grout re-stains in eleven days. We need a strict, visible standard.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Midori,,"@May, I see the friction now. The chat rows started with reminders, and the previous tenants stopped speaking by year two. We must avoid that silence.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji, two hours is too long for a casual pass. We need to split the tasks to keep individual shifts under forty minutes.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Toshio, splitting it helps, but the firm’s terms mean I still need to be present for two hours. That is a significant block of my day.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, splitting is logical, but presence is the variable. If two are gone, the remaining three carry the load. We must weight the rotation by actual days present, not just names.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, weighting by presence is smart, but I need the standard to be non-negotiable. If ""done"" is vague, the rotation fails.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@May, I agree. A clear standard prevents the resentment that silenced the previous tenants. We need to define ""done"" so no one feels shortchanged.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, weighting by presence is fair, but the 2,300 yen in duplicate purchases is a leak. We need a single buyer to stop the waste.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Toshio, I agree on the single buyer. But my main concern is the two-hour block. If we outsource, I still lose that time. I need to know if we can split the firm’s visit.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Ryuji, splitting the firm’s visit is a logistical nightmare. My data shows the mess is concentrated. We should target the kitchen, not the whole house, to save time.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, targeting the kitchen is good, but the bathroom is my nightmare. I need a strict, visible checklist so I never have to guess again.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@May, a visible checklist is essential. It removes the guesswork and prevents the silent resentment that broke the last group.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"@May, a checklist is good, but I need the financials settled. I will propose a shared pot to stop the duplicate buying and track who owes what.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Toshio, a shared pot is fine, but it doesn't solve the time block. I need to know if we can stagger the firm’s arrival to avoid the two-hour dead zone.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Ryuji, staggering is impossible with their terms. My data shows the kitchen is the bottleneck. Let’s focus there to cut the time, not just split it.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, focusing on the kitchen ignores my bathroom anxiety. I need a strict, visible checklist for the bathroom to stop the guessing game.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Midori,,"@May, I hear you. A clear checklist protects the bathroom, but we must also protect our relationships. Let’s ensure the rules keep us talking, not just cleaning.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
